Dyson's direct repair service model offers a vertically integrated approach to product maintenance that extends appliance lifespans. Dyson employs over 900 dedicated repair engineers globally who service products using only genuine parts, with many repairs completed within 72 hours. The company designs its products with serviceability in mind — key wear components like motors, filters, and batteries are modular and replaceable without specialised tools. Dyson's online diagnostic tool guides users through troubleshooting before escalating to professional repair, reducing unnecessary service calls by approximately 40%. The company maintains a ten-year spare parts commitment for all products and has invested in refurbishment centres that process returned units for resale through official 'Dyson Outlet' channels at reduced prices. The service infrastructure is supported by product passports: each machine's serial number links to its full maintenance and repair history, enabling informed decisions about repair versus replacement.